.TH CODEXBAR-LINUXD 1 "2026-05-04" "codexbar-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codexbar-linuxd \- user-scoped CodexBar GNOME daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codexbar-linuxd
[\fB--version\fR] [\fB--check\fR] [\fB--print-snapshot\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codexbar-linuxd
is the user-scoped daemon for CodexBar GNOME. It exposes the
.B org.codexbar.Linux1
session D-Bus API used by the GNOME Shell extension, keeps normalized local
cache and settings, and invokes the upstream
.B codexbar
CLI for supported provider usage and cost snapshots.
.PP
The daemon is intended to be started through D-Bus activation or the packaged
systemd user service. It does not open a TCP listener and does not enable the
GNOME Shell extension.
.PP
Credential import, profile discovery, desktop secret-store access, dashboard
collection, browser integration, and local network APIs are outside the v0.1
data plane.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the daemon binary name and package version, then exit.
.TP
.B --check
Validate daemon startup prerequisites and exit.
.TP
.B --print-snapshot
Print the current normalized snapshot JSON and exit. This is primarily useful
for local diagnostics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/codexbar-linux/config.json
Daemon-owned user settings.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/codexbar-linux/snapshot.json
Normalized snapshot cache.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.codexbar.Linux1.service
Packaged D-Bus session activation file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/codexbar-linuxd.service
Packaged systemd user service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR busctl (1),
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
